sn4.6:5.1 starts: “Though many creatures crawl about,
sn4.6:5.2 starts: Many terrors, flies, serpents,
sn4.6:5.3 starts: The great sage gone to his empty hut
sn4.6:5.4 starts: Stirs not a hair because of them.
sn45.4:11.1 starts: “This divine vehicle unsurpassed
sn45.4:11.2 starts: Originates from within oneself.
sn45.4:11.3 starts: The wise depart from the world in it,
sn45.4:11.4 starts: Inevitably winning the victory.”
